  data: {
    LLM: "1. Deal: Each player and the dealer receives seven cards. 2. Split: Players divide cards into a 5-card back hand and a 2-card front hand. 3. Constraint: The 5-card hand must always outrank the 2-card hand. 4. Reveal: Hands are compared against the banker's hands. 5. Scoring: Win both to win; lose both to lose; split one each for a push. Ties favor the banker.",
    Player: "1. Deal: Each player and the dealer receives seven cards. 2. Split: Players divide cards into a 5-card back hand and a 2-card front hand. 3. Constraint: The 5-card hand must always outrank the 2-card hand. 4. Reveal: Hands are compared against the banker's hands. 5. Scoring: Win both to win; lose both to lose; split one each for a push. Ties favor the banker.",
    objective: "Arrange seven cards into two separate poker hands that both outrank the dealer's corresponding hands.",
    gameplay: "1. Deal: Each player and the dealer receives seven cards. 2. Split: Players divide cards into a 5-card back hand and a 2-card front hand. 3. Constraint: The 5-card hand must always outrank the 2-card hand. 4. Reveal: Hands are compared against the banker's hands. 5. Scoring: Win both to win; lose both to lose; split one each for a push. Ties favor the banker.",
    keyRules: [
      'The 5-card hand rank must exceed the 2-card hand rank or the hand is fouled.',
      "Winner must beat both of the banker's hands; losing one results in a push.",
      'Ties on individual hand comparisons (copies) are won by the banker.',
      'Joker completes straights or flushes in the high hand; otherwise it is an Ace.',
      'Wheel straight (A-2-3-4-5) is typically ranked as the second-highest straight.',
    ],
